{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `log_radon`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual `target += normal_lpdf(log_radon[n] | mu[n], sigma_y)` likelihood loop with a single vectorized built-in sampling statement, `log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y)`. The predictor vector `mu` is still computed deterministically from `alpha` and `county_idx` before observing `log_radon`. No data fields were added or changed; `N`, `J`, and `county_idx` remain context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> J;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county_idx;
  vector[N] log_radon;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] alpha;
  real mu_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
}
model {
  vector[N] mu;

  // priors
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_alpha ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_alpha ~ normal(0, 10);

  // hierarchical prior
  alpha ~ normal(mu_alpha, sigma_alpha);

  // likelihood
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    mu[n] = alpha[county_idx[n]];
  }
  log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":4,"N":2,"county_idx":[2,2],"log_radon":[6.134671501894284,6.881518693048437]}","protected_variables":["log_radon"]}
